{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791648663,"nonce":"G5XZR1z3+RGsL1zpUJ1oduA73J4=","title":"Module-level fields are broken: lower them as statics of a per-module class","message":"Conformance row TestModuleStatics (Haxe 4.2+ module-level fields). Probed on the row's\nown declarations: string finals print `0 1 2 3`, assigning a module `var` gives\ngarbage, reassigning a module `dynamic function` has no effect, and\n`@:isVar var prop(get,set)` never calls its accessors (the parser's ModuleFieldKind\ncannot represent properties). These go through TypedModuleFieldKind::Var into HIR\nglobal variables (tast_to_hir.rs lower_module_field).\n\nHaxe models them as public statics of a synthetic per-module class; do the same so\nbare names in the module, `pack.Module.field` paths, dynamic functions and properties\nall reuse the static machinery. The row also needs Context.defineModule and TDField\nin defineType (a patch exists: scratchpad pModStatics.diff, conflicts with\ncontext_api.rs since batch 25).","files":null}]}